{"id": 61, "ts": 1780601494.6870763, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s reminder of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s flawless reliability and calm decision\u2011making, but the concerns about his egocentric attitude and difficulty communicating ideas remain unaddressed and could directly undermine crew cooperation in a long\u2011haul cockpit. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strengths are well\u2011documented: he is very conscientious, handles stress very well, assesses weather accurately, and has excellent computer skills\u2014key technical competencies for international routes. While he can be pretentious and sometimes adopts the wrong tone, those communication flaws are less severe than a pilot who may struggle to convey critical information during a crisis. Moreover, we have no evidence of Candidate\u202fA\u2019s stress\u2011resilience (Sarah confirmed no observations) and no concrete data on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation (James noted only potential hindrances from a hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude). Given the lack of positive evidence for A and D, and the balanced profile of B, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fB**."}
